---
import Layout from "@/layouts/main.astro";
---

<Layout 
  title="Terms & Conditions (Draft) - RS Prints"
  description="General terms, conditions of service, ordering policies, returns, and disclaimers."
  canonicalUrl="/terms-and-conditions"
  currentActive="terms"
>
  <main class="container mx-auto px-4 py-8 md:py-12 max-w-4xl flex-1 flex flex-col gap-8">
    <!-- Header Section -->
    <div class="border-b border-border pb-6">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 mb-3">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider bg-amber-500/15 text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400 border border-amber-500/30">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-3.5 h-3.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3Z"/>
            <line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"/>
            <line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"/>
          </svg>
          Dummy / Placeholder Document
        </span>
        <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground font-mono">
          Last updated: February 13, 2026 (Draft)
        </span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-2xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground">
        General Terms & Conditions
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-2 leading-relaxed">
        Please read these terms and conditions carefully before accessing, using, or placing orders through this platform.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Dummy Flag / Draft Notice Banner -->
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-500/10 dark:bg-amber-950/20 p-4 md:p-5 flex gap-4 text-amber-950 dark:text-amber-200">
      <div class="shrink-0 mt-0.5">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
          <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
          <line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/>
          <line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-1 text-xs md:text-sm leading-relaxed">
        <p class="font-semibold text-foreground">
          Notice: Placeholder / Sample Document (Pending Formal Execution)
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          This document is an illustrative draft template prepared for staging and preview purposes. All original third-party and external business entity names, addresses, and individual contact handles have been sanitized and replaced with generalized placeholders (e.g., <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-foreground">[Company / Registered Entity Name]</code>). This template does not yet constitute an executed or binding legal document until finalized by our legal counsel.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Content Sections -->
    <div class="text-xs md:text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground space-y-8 font-sans">
      
      <!-- Section 1 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>1.</span> Acceptance of General Terms & Conditions
        </h2>
        <p>
          Thank you for visiting <span class="text-primary font-medium">[https://yourwebsite.com]</span> (“Site”). Please read these General Terms and Conditions (“Terms”) carefully. In these Terms, the term "you", “your” refers to the user or viewer of the Site and the terms “[Company Name]”, “our”, “us”, “we” refers to <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company / Registered Entity Name]</span>, a company incorporated under the relevant applicable laws, and includes its authorized affiliates. These Terms govern your access and use of this Site, which is hosted and operated by <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company / Registered Entity Name]</span>, having its registered office at <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Registered Office Address, City, State, PIN Code, Country]</span>.
        </p>
        <p>
          By accessing and/or using this Site, you confirm that you are competent to contract under the relevant local laws and that you agree to be bound by these Terms and to any additional guidelines, restrictions, or rules that may be posted in connection with specific sections or services of this Site. All such additional posted guidelines, restrictions, or rules are hereby incorporated by reference into these Terms. <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span> reserves the right to make changes to the Site and/or update these Terms at its discretion at any time without prior notice. Any change or modification to the Terms will be effective from the date of such update on the Site. Your continued use of the Site following the modifications to the Terms constitutes your acceptance of the modified Terms.
        </p>
        <p>
          You further agree that we may provide all legal communications and notices to you electronically by posting them on our Site or, at our election, by sending an e-mail to the e-mail address provided by you when you registered on our Site. You may withdraw your consent to receive communications electronically by contacting our customer care. However, if you withdraw your consent to receive communications electronically, you must discontinue your use of your account.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>2.</span> Eligibility to Use
        </h2>
        <p>
          Use of the Site is available only to such persons who can legally contract under applicable contract laws (including the Indian Contract Act, 1872 or equivalent local statutes). Persons who are "incompetent to contract", including minors or un-discharged insolvents, shall not be eligible to use the Site independently.
        </p>
        <p>
          Any minor desirous to use or transact on the Site is required to conduct such transaction only through their legal guardian or parents.
        </p>
        <p>
          By accepting the Terms or using or transacting on the Site, you irrevocably declare and undertake that you are of legal age (i.e., 18 years or older), of sound mind, and capable of entering into a binding contract. Such usage shall be deemed to form a binding contract between the Site and the User to the extent permissible under applicable laws.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>3.</span> Intellectual Property Rights
        </h2>
        <p>
          This Site contains graphics, photographs, images, document layouts, artwork, text, fonts, video, audio, software tools, stock assets, and other information (referred to herein as “[Platform Content]”). This Site and all [Platform Content] are the intellectual property of <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span> and/or its licensors. All rights in this Site and [Platform Content] are reserved worldwide. It is strictly prohibited to sell, license, rent, modify, retain, copy, reproduce, distribute, publish, or use any portion of the [Platform Content] except to the extent expressly allowed in these Terms.
        </p>
        <p>
          <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span> reserves the right to add to, delete from, or modify any part of [Platform Content] at any time without prior notice. You acknowledge that such modification may result in you losing access to any [Platform Content] saved or accessible by you by virtue of being registered on the Site, including any content uploaded by you for creating any Product to be ordered. Any modifications to [Platform Content] remain the property of <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span> and/or its licensors.
        </p>
        <p>
          Except as otherwise provided for in the specific Product offer itself, any design tools, templates, and services provided on this Site employ a limited number of elements, including icons, fonts, colour schemes, and design effects. <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span> reserves the right to use all such elements and make them available for use by other parties in the future. You agree to access and use the Site, [Platform Content], and design tools strictly in accordance with these Terms.
        </p>
        <p>
          You acknowledge that by creating an account or using the design tools, you do not obtain any exclusive right or trademark claim to any individual design elements or template designs available on the Site. Other customers may use the same design tools and template designs to create designs, logos, or merchandise having similar or identical combinations of elements. <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span> provides no warranty of any kind that designs created using our tools will not infringe, or be subject to a claim of infringing, any trademark or other intellectual property rights of another party. It is solely your responsibility to obtain independent legal advice regarding whether your design is legally available for your use.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>4.</span> Use of Site & User Content
        </h2>
        <p>
          Before placing an order online or accessing certain services or features on this Site, you may need a user account. You are granted permission to access and use this Site and [Platform Content] solely for the purpose of preparing, creating, designing, evaluating, and ordering products or services directly through <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span> (referred to herein as “Products”). No other download, retention, publication, or commercial distribution of any portion of [Platform Content] is authorized or permitted.
        </p>
        <p>
          You represent, warrant, and confirm that where the Products contain any text, image, design, trademark, service mark, or copyrighted work of any third party, you have obtained appropriate permission, consent, no-objection, or authorization from such third party for such use prior to ordering, and shall provide proof of authorization to <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span> upon request.
        </p>
        <p>
          You further represent and warrant that Products ordered by you do not infringe upon any third-party rights, including copyright, trademark, trade name, or privacy, and will not libel, defame, harass, stalk, threaten, or violate the legal rights of any party. You agree not to submit, upload, or request printing of any content or design associated with government bodies, public authorities, financial institutions, or regulated entities without verifiable official authorization.
        </p>
        <p>
          You agree not to upload or order any Product displaying content which is:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
          <li>In violation of the Emblems and Names (Prevention of Improper Use) Act, 1950 or relevant national heraldic emblems regulations;</li>
          <li>Falsely depicting any person as an official representative of a constituency under The Representation of the People Act, 1951 or equivalent election statutes;</li>
          <li>Offensive, unlawful, harassing, defamatory, obscene, indecent, malicious, or abusive.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span> reserves the right in its sole discretion, without prior notice, to refuse to accept, print, or maintain any images, artwork, text, or content uploaded by you (“User Content”), or to cancel any order without assigning any reason. Where unlawful activity is suspected, we reserve the right to report such incidents to appropriate law enforcement authorities.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>5.</span> Taxes & GST
        </h2>
        <p>
          You agree to pay Goods and Services Tax (GST) or other applicable taxes, whether international, national, state, or local, levied or imposed with respect to any Product ordered by you on the Site.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where applicable, you agree to mention your valid GST registration number and Entity Name during checkout. You must ensure that the GST registration number and Entity Name match the billing address provided, as modifications to these details cannot be processed once the order has been submitted.
        </p>
        <p>
          <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span> is not responsible for independent verification of your GST registration details. Any tax liability or forfeiture of input tax credit resulting from incorrect details shall be borne entirely by you. In the event you fail to provide a GST number at checkout, the transaction will be treated as an unregistered consumer order. In all circumstances, our liability under GST shall be strictly limited to the amount of tax collected on the invoice.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 6 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>6.</span> Shipping and Delivery
        </h2>
        <p>
          All Products purchased from the Site shall be delivered to you by our appointed third-party logistics partners.
        </p>
        <p>
          We endeavor to make our best efforts to ensure timely delivery on the Estimated Arrival Date indicated during order placement. However, Estimated Arrival Dates are purely indicative. <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span> cannot accept liability or be held financially responsible for delays caused by adverse weather, flight schedules, carrier strikes, geopolitical occurrences, regional entry restrictions, or other force majeure circumstances.
        </p>
        <p>
          You undertake to provide an accurate and complete postal address, PIN code, and contact number. We cannot be held liable for misdirected, delayed, or lost shipments resulting from incomplete or inaccurate address information provided during checkout.
        </p>
        <p>
          In the event you are unavailable for delivery or refuse acceptance upon repeated delivery attempts within a 7-day period, <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span> shall be entitled to return or dispose of the customized products, without liability for refund or post-disposal claims.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 7 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>7.</span> Cash on Delivery (COD)
        </h2>
        <p>
          Cash on delivery may be offered for select eligible PIN codes and order categories. The facility is confirmed only if your postal area is serviceable by our logistics partners.
        </p>
        <p>
          Payment under COD must be tendered in cash or by accepted card upon delivery. By selecting COD, you commit to pay the specified invoice amount on delivery. In cases of split shipments or excess collection confirmed by our logistics partner, refunds of excess cash will be credited to the verified bank account provided by you.
        </p>
        <p>
          We reserve the right to suspend accounts, refuse future COD privileges, or initiate appropriate recovery remedies against users who place orders and unjustifiably refuse delivery.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 8 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>8.</span> Pricing Policy
        </h2>
        <p>
          All prices, fees, discounts, and promotional offers posted on the Site are subject to change without notice and are not guaranteed indefinitely. Placing a Product in your cart does not reserve or freeze the price shown at that moment. The price charged will be the price in effect at the time the order is formally confirmed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 9 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>9.</span> Refunds, Payments & Store Credits
        </h2>
        <p>
          Refunds, where approved, shall normally be processed back to the original source payment method (bank account, credit/debit card, UPI, or digital wallet). For Cash on Delivery transactions, refunds may be remitted to your bank account via NEFT upon provision of valid bank account details.
        </p>
        <p>
          Refunds may take up to 7 to 15 business days to reflect depending on your banking institution. Upon request, we will provide the Acquirer Reference Number (ARN) or Unique Transaction Reference (UTR) for refund tracking.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you elect to receive Merchant Store Credit in lieu of a bank refund, such credit will remain valid for forty-five (45) days from the date of issuance, after which any unutilized credit balance shall lapse.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 10 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>10.</span> Product Issues & Claims Timeline
        </h2>
        <p>
          Any manufacturing defects, printing errors, or transit damages must be reported to our customer support within <span class="font-semibold text-foreground">15 calendar days</span> of receiving your order, accompanied by clear photographic or video evidence. Claims reported beyond this period cannot be entertained.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 11 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>11.</span> Return Pickup
        </h2>
        <p>
          Where a physical return is requested to process an approved claim, our logistics partner will make up to three (3) pickup attempts at your registered address. If the parcel is not handed over within these three attempts, the pickup request will be marked as failed and closed.
        </p>
        <p>
          Returned items undergo standard quality verification upon arrival at our warehouse before refunds or reprint orders are released.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 12 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>12.</span> Transfer of Title
        </h2>
        <p>
          Risk of loss and title for any physical printed Product pass to you upon delivery of the consignment to our carrier. For any digital deliverables or electronic formats, delivery is deemed completed at the time the digital file or download link is transmitted to your registered email address or account dashboard.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 13 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>13.</span> Indemnification
        </h2>
        <p>
          You agree to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span>, its directors, officers, employees, suppliers, and partners from and against all claims, liabilities, losses, expenses, damages, and legal costs arising out of: (i) your breach of these Terms; (ii) any infringement of intellectual property, copyright, trademark, or privacy rights arising from artwork, photos, or text uploaded or commissioned by you; or (iii) any unlawful use of the ordered merchandise.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 14 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>14.</span> Disclaimer of Warranty & Customer Proofing
        </h2>
        <p class="uppercase font-mono text-[11px] border border-border/80 p-3.5 bg-secondary/10 rounded-lg text-foreground leading-normal">
          THE SITE AND ALL PLATFORM CONTENT ARE PROVIDED "AS IS" WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EITHER EXPRESSED OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, OR NON-INFRINGEMENT.
        </p>
        <p>
          Please note that <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span> does not proofread or manually edit customer documents before production. You are solely responsible for reviewing and proofing your designs prior to placing an order. We cannot be held liable for:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
          <li>Spelling, grammatical, typographical, or punctuation mistakes made by the customer;</li>
          <li>Low resolution, blurry, or pixilated graphics submitted by the customer;</li>
          <li>Layout errors, bleed oversights, or margin discrepancies introduced during creation;</li>
          <li>Customer-selected options such as paper finish, sizing, or quantity choices;</li>
          <li>Damage resulting from improper handling after final delivery.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 15 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>15.</span> Limitation of Liability
        </h2>
        <p>
          Under no circumstances shall <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span>, its directors, employees, or suppliers be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages, loss of business, data, or anticipated profits arising out of or in connection with the use of the Site or our manufactured products, even if advised of the possibility of such damages. In all events, our total cumulative liability shall not exceed the actual purchase price paid by you for the specific Product giving rise to the claim.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 16 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>16.</span> Site Feedback
        </h2>
        <p>
          Any suggestions, feedback, reviews, or ideas submitted regarding our website or service shall be deemed non-confidential and will become the sole property of <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Company Name]</span> without entitlement to compensation or attribution.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 17 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>17.</span> Grievance & Nodal Officer Details
        </h2>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-border bg-card/60 space-y-1.5 text-xs md:text-sm">
          <p><span class="font-semibold text-foreground">Officer Name / Designation:</span> [Grievance / Nodal Officer Name]</p>
          <p><span class="font-semibold text-foreground">Email:</span> <a href="mailto:grievance@yourdomain.com" class="text-primary hover:underline font-mono">[grievance@yourdomain.com]</a></p>
          <p><span class="font-semibold text-foreground">Customer Support Contact:</span> <span class="font-mono">[+91 XXXXX XXXXX]</span> (Mon-Sat, 9:30 AM - 6:30 PM IST)</p>
          <p><span class="font-semibold text-foreground">Help Center / Portal:</span> <a href="#" class="text-primary hover:underline font-mono">[https://yourwebsite.com/help-centre]</a></p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 18 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>18.</span> Dispute Resolution
        </h2>
        <p>
          In the event of any query, grievance, or dispute arising out of or in connection with these Terms, the parties shall first make genuine, reasonable efforts to resolve the dispute amicably. The attempt to reach an amicable resolution shall be treated as having concluded if the dispute remains unsettled after thirty (30) days from the date of written notice served by either party.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 19 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base md:text-lg font-heading font-semibold text-foreground tracking-wide flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>19.</span> Governing Law & Jurisdiction
        </h2>
        <p>
          These Terms and all matters arising out of or related to your use of this Site or transactions conducted herein shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[State / Country, e.g., India]</span>. Subject to amicable resolution, the courts situated at <span class="font-medium text-foreground">[Designated City / Jurisdiction]</span> shall possess exclusive jurisdiction over any legal proceedings arising from these Terms.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
